ehearsal fault found and traced:** one parallel control run failed 47 of 48.\n   138\t  - The swap test exchanged P01 and P02. In about 2 of 26 shuffles, these are two draws of the same unit and arm.\n   139\t  - The rehearsal's draws answer alike, so their text is identical and the swap changes nothing.\n   140\t  - That is harmless to the verdict, which counts by unit, not by draw. The test now swaps two different units.\n   141\t- **Mutants:** 19 of 19 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   142\t  - Three missed in the first run and were traced:\n   143\t    - one was stale, because packets now render from the attempts;\n   144\t    - one was masked by the shared-only filter, and a shared within-call case was added;\n   145\t    - one disabled only half a condition.\n   146\t  - One mutant is equivalent and is left out: unifying any key across calls, not only declared shared ones. C3 looks only at\n   147\t    forecasts reachable from each member's own outcome, so the result does not change.\n   148\t\n   149\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n   150\t\n   151\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n   152\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n   153\t  - Each packet shows the questions, every passage a figure or citation names (as the request showed it), the figures and the cards.\n   154\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. Its cards cannot count as usable.\n   155\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n   156\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n   157\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n   158\t  2. **contradiction:**