''v9'\\\\'']['\\\\''attempts'\\\\''].insert(0,bad)\nbody,_,_=pg.packet_body(items,pair,'\\\\''separate'\\\\'','\\\\''publish'\\\\'',cards)\nprint('\\\\''a single-card retry is visible'\\\\'',[(x.strip()) for x in body if x.startswith('\\\\''###'\\\\'') or x.strip().startswith('\\\\''Attempt'\\\\'')])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"started & torn attempt {'decision': 'interrupted', 'attempts': []} [{'line': 2, 'text': '{\"unit\":\"single-E\",\"arm\"'}]   No attempt was made.\na single-card retry is visible ['### Card K1: How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\\n  Ladder: rung 1: Total revenue is at least $450 billion. / rung 2: Total revenue is at least $400 billion but less than $450 billion. / rung 3: Total revenue is at least $350 billion but less than $400 billion. / rung 4: Total revenue is at least $300 billion but less than $350 billion. / rung 5: Total revenue is less than $300 billion.', 'Attempt 1 (final): accepted by the checks', '### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\\n  Ladder: rung 1: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $450 billion. / rung 2: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $400 billion and below $450 billion. / rung 3: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion. / rung 4: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion. / rung 5: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is below $300 billion.', 'Attempt 1: refused by the checks', 'Attempt 2 (final): accepted by the checks']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"NOT READY\n\n1. **A packet swap can still change the verdict without changing any checked digest.** In a 27-packet replay, a joint packet and a separate packet from the same snapshot rendered identically. Swapping their key entries left the run, packet text, and readings untouched, but changed PASS (9–5) to STOP (8–6). Seal the packet-to-unit, arm, and draw mapping before readers receive the packets, and verify that seal at verdict time. [Packet binding](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:541) · [Verdict](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:582)\n\n2. **Reconciliation can still erase duplicates from one call.** In an R1 replay, the second call contained two equal Q4 forecasts. The merge aliased both to the first call’s forecast, and the pair passed. Keeping those duplicates made C4 refuse it. Unify a shared forecast only when each call has exactly one candidate for that quantity and scenario. [Merge](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:305)\n\n3. **Retry histories still reveal the arm.** A packet showed one card accepted on attempt one and the other accepted on attempt two. That pattern can only come from separate calls. Score final pairs without retry histories, then present earlier attempts separately under blind labels for diagnostic reading. [Packet rendering](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:482)\n\n4. **Recovery misreports an interrupted attempt.** With a valid `started` record and a torn completion line, recovery correctly marked the unit `interrupted`, but its packet said “No attempt was made.” Preserve the started attempt in the packet and distinguish interruption from a request that never started. [Final status derivation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:223) · [Packet status](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:483)"}}
